      "anchor": "page",
      "anchorLabel": "General",
      "anchorText": "",
      "text": "This is my ideation page, I want htis page to just focus on getting me the ideas. \n\nSo we should have the plan for that. \nAnd in different tabs we should have the runs we make from the inputs you require for me.",
      "kind": "note",
      "status": "sent",
      "ts": "2026-10-01T02:58:19.040888+00:00",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "claude",
          "t": "2026-10-01T03:00:51.300738+00:00",
          "text": "Done. This page is now **Ideation**, with 4 tabs: **Plan** (how ideation works, plus rubric v3), **Inputs** (moved here from the old inputs page, with your answers carried over), **Sources** (the tested list and S1\u2013S3), and **Run 3**. Each future run gets its own tab. The old inputs page is retired (moved to the Trash). Run 3 is ready to start whenever you say."
        }
      ],
      "addressed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "c1790823849039",
      "anchor": "page",
      "anchorLabel": "General",
      "anchorText": "",
      "text": "Why the send decisions is highlighted when nothing is queued etc.",
      "kind": "note",
      "status": "sent",
      "ts": "2026-10-01T03:04:09.042940+00:00",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "claude",
          "t": "2026-10-01T03:04:20.635503+00:00",
          "text": "That was my doing. When I moved your answers over from the old inputs page, I saved them here as 5 new decisions (I1\u2013I6). Send counted them as changed since round 3, so it lit up, even though you hadn't changed anything yourself. Round 4 has now recorded them, so after a reload Send should show **Nothing new to send** until you change something."
        }
      ],
      "addressed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "c1790824799885",
      "anchor": "page",
      "anchorLabel": "General",
      "anchorText": "",
      "text": "I feel this is less intuitive.\nSend decisions (round 7)\n\nIt should say \nSend 1 Decisons, 2 Comments, 1 Questions and 4 Changes. \n\nAnd when we haven't done anything it should say Notinh to send. \n\nWhy are you making this mistake again and again?",
      "kind": "note",
      "status": "sent",
      "ts": "2026-10-01T03:19:59.888834+00:00",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "claude",
          "t": "2026-10-01T03:22:33.502766+00:00",
          "text": "You're right, and sorry for the repeat. Three causes, all fixed and tested in your Chrome: **1)** every time I carried your answers over, I saved them myself, and Send counted my saves as *your* changes (rounds 4, 6 and 7). The server now lets me save without that, and I'll always use it. **2)** The label never said what it sends. It now reads e.g. **Send 1 decision, 2 comments, 3 changes**, or **Nothing to send**. Questions aren't counted, because they go to me instantly. **3)** This round, the page-update tool also broke the tabs code. That's fixed too. The fix is in the html-worker skill, so every page gets it."
        }
      ],
      "addressed": true
    }
  ],
